<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15490" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-linguis</span></b> , e, adj.
		lingua. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>deprived of a
			tongue</i>, <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 23, 14</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Hist. Eccl. 6,
			15</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen., <i>speechless</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 10, 22</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				10, 19</span></i> (with mutus); <i><span class="en">id.
				post Red. 3, 7</span></i> (with mutus and tacitus); <i><span class="en">Gell. 5, 1,
				9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Pregn., <i>without eloquence</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut.
				26, 100</span></i>; Cels. praef. <i>med.</i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tac. Or. 36 <i>fin.</i></span></i> (opp. disertus).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
